--- rust-template/.lycheeignore
+++ .lycheeignore
@@ -1,12 +1,19 @@
-# Lychee ignore patterns - regex patterns for URLs to skip during link checking
+# Patterns (regular expressions) that .github/workflows/links.yml excludes from
+# the external link check. Every entry needs the comment above it saying why the
+# link is unreachable from a runner but still correct in the document -- the
+# workflow-hygiene test fails on an uncommented line, so nothing can be muted
+# silently.
 
-# Localhost and local development URLs
-https?://localhost
-https?://127\.0\.0\.1
+# npmjs.com answers every unauthenticated non-browser request with 403, whether
+# the package exists or not:
+#   curl -sIL -o /dev/null -w '%{http_code}\n' https://www.npmjs.com/package/command-stream
+#   403
+# The README badges and the comparison table link there on purpose.
+^https://(www\.)?npmjs\.com/
 
-# Example and placeholder URLs used by the template
-https?://example\.com
-https://docs\.rs/example-sum-package-name
-
-# Web Archive rejects automated checks despite serving browser requests
-https://web\.archive\.org
+# GitHub serves the stargazers list and every /settings/ page only to a signed-in
+# session; anonymously both answer 404 even for this public repository:
+#   curl -sIL -o /dev/null -w '%{http_code}\n' https://github.com/link-foundation/command-stream/stargazers
+#   404
+# docs/CI-CD.md links to the settings page as the place a maintainer has to visit.
+^https://github\.com/link-foundation/command-stream/(stargazers|settings/)
